.TH "ODOO-WORK-CLI-CLOCK-LIST" "1" "" "odoo-work-cli" "odoo-work-cli manual"
.\" Generated by `mise run docs:reference` from the CLI's help texts. Do not edit.
.SH NAME
odoo\-work\-cli\-clock\-list \- List attendance records of a day or week
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "odoo\-work\-cli clock list"
[\-\-date\ YYYY\-MM\-DD\ |\ \-\-week\ YYYY\-Www] [\-\-json\ |\ \-\-format\ FORMAT]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the attendance records of a day (\-\-date, default today) or an ISO
week (\-\-week YYYY\-Www) with ID, check\-in, check\-out and duration.
.PP
Records are attributed to the day of their check\-in. A record that crosses
midnight is listed on its check\-in day and shows the check\-out date. Use it
before 'clock edit' to see what is already recorded.
.PP
\-\-date and \-\-week together are a validation error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR \fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR
Day to list, YYYY\-MM\-DD.
.br
\fIstring; optional; default: today\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-week\fR \fIYYYY\-Www\fR
ISO week to list, YYYY\-Www.
.br
\fIstring; optional\fR
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output FORMAT: table, json or jsonl.
.br
\fIone of table, json, jsonl; optional; default: table\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.br
\fIflag; optional\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fIBACKEND\fR
BACKEND: odoo or fake (offline, made\-up data; env ODOO_WORK_CLI_BACKEND).
.br
\fIstring; optional; default: odoo; env: ODOO_WORK_CLI_BACKEND\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Read only the config FILE (skip discovery).
.br
\fIstring; optional\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of the command and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
The columns ID, Check In, Check Out (with the date if it is on a later
day, \-\-:\-\- while running) and Duration (H:MM, "(running)" for a running
record), then the total; or "No attendance records."
.PP
With \-\-json an array of attendance records, oldest first, [] if there are
none.
.PP
Fields of attendance.schema.json:
.TP
\fBid\fR
\fIinteger\fR
.TP
\fBemployee_id\fR
\fIinteger or null\fR
.TP
\fBemployee\fR
\fIstring or null\fR
.TP
\fBcheck_in\fR
\fIstring (RFC 3339 timestamp)\fR
.TP
\fBcheck_out\fR
\fIstring (RFC 3339 timestamp) or null\fR
.TP
\fBrunning\fR
\fIboolean\fR
.TP
\fBworked_hours\fR
\fInumber\fR
.TP
\fBworked_minutes\fR
\fIinteger\fR
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBODOO_URL\fR
Odoo server URL; overrides url from the config files.
.TP
\fBODOO_DATABASE\fR
Odoo database name; overrides database.
.TP
\fBODOO_USERNAME\fR
Odoo login, usually an e\-mail address; overrides username.
.TP
\fBODOO_PASSWORD\fR
Odoo API key, used for XML\-RPC. Despite the name, not the login password.
.TP
\fBODOO_WEB_PASSWORD\fR
Odoo login password, used for the web session of clock in and clock out.
.TP
\fBODOO_TOTP_SECRET\fR
TOTP secret (base32 or otpauth:// URL) for accounts with two\-factor authentication.
.TP
\fBODOO_OP_TIMEOUT\fR
Timeout of the 1Password call that resolves [op_secrets], a Go duration; default 5s.
.TP
\fBODOO_WORK_CLI_NO_OP\fR
If 1, true, yes or on, [op_secrets] is ignored and the 1Password CLI is never called.
.TP
\fBODOO_WORK_CLI_BACKEND\fR
Backend, odoo (default) or fake; \-\-backend overrides it.
.TP
\fBODOO_WORK_CLI_FAKE_STATE\fR
State file of the fake backend; default odoo\-work\-cli\-fake\-state.json in the temporary directory.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
Base directory of the global config file; default ~/.config.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/odoo\-work\-cli/config.toml\fR
Global configuration ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/odoo\-work\-cli/config.toml if XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set). Created by odoo\-work\-cli config install.
.TP
\fB\&.odoo\-work\-cli.toml\fR
Configuration of a directory tree. Every such file from the filesystem root down to the current directory is merged over the global file, the deepest last. \-\-config FILE loads only FILE instead.
.TP
\fB$TMPDIR/odoo\-work\-cli\-fake\-state.json\fR
State of the fake backend (\-\-backend fake); ODOO_WORK_CLI_FAKE_STATE sets another path. Delete it to start over with the seed data.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error, including usage errors. With \-\-json or \-\-format json|jsonl the error is printed on standard output as one JSON object, {"error": {"kind": KIND, "message": TEXT}}, and nothing on standard error; otherwise as "Error: TEXT" on standard error, after usage errors followed by the usage.
.PP
Error kinds this command can fail with:
.TP
\fBauth\fR
Authentication failed: wrong API key or login password, TOTP rejected.
.TP
\fBvalidation\fR
Invalid input: unknown flag, bad argument, malformed date, time or hours, a time in the future, an unknown project.
.TP
\fBnetwork\fR
Odoo cannot be reached: DNS, connection refused, timeout, TLS.
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
The local configuration is missing or invalid.
.TP
\fBsecrets_locked\fR
1Password is locked or unreachable, so op:// references could not be resolved.
.TP
\fBinternal\fR
Anything else: an unexpected Odoo response or a bug.
.SH EXAMPLES
A week, with the total:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ odoo\-work\-cli clock list \-\-week 2026\-W14
ID      Check In         Check Out        Duration
\-\-\-\-\-\-\- \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
4601    2026\-03\-30 08:30 16:45            8:15
4602    2026\-03\-31 08:15 16:30            8:15
4603    2026\-04\-01 08:20 16:20            8:00
4604    2026\-04\-02 08:00 15:00            7:00

Total: 31:30
.fi
.RE
.PP
One day as JSON:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ odoo\-work\-cli clock list \-\-date 2026\-04\-08 \-\-json
[
  {
    "id": 4606,
    "employee_id": 7,
    "employee": "Alex Demo",
    "check_in": "2026\-04\-08T08:30:00+02:00",
    "check_out": "2026\-04\-08T12:00:00+02:00",
    "running": false,
    "worked_hours": 3.5,
    "worked_minutes": 210
  },
  {
    "id": 4607,
    "employee_id": 7,
    "employee": "Alex Demo",
    "check_in": "2026\-04\-08T12:30:00+02:00",
    "check_out": "2026\-04\-08T17:00:00+02:00",
    "running": false,
    "worked_hours": 4.5,
    "worked_minutes": 270
  }
]
.fi
.RE
